course: dictionary
lesson: 7285
title: Pinpoint: exact and small
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Pinpoint can do three jobs. As a verb, to pinpoint something means to find or show its exact place, cause or time. «Each cat ear has about 30 muscles and can turn on its own to pinpoint a sound» means the ear can turn to find exactly where a sound is coming from.
explain: As a noun, a pinpoint is a very small dot, like the point of a pin: "a pinpoint of light". As an adjective, pinpoint means very exact, as in "pinpoint accuracy".
explain: To work out which job the word does, read the words around it. Ask: is it showing a place, a tiny dot, or how exact something is? Then swap in your meaning to check the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Pinpoint can be a verb, a noun or an adjective.
fact: As a verb, «pinpoint» means to find or show the exact place, cause or time of something.
fact: As a noun, «a pinpoint» means a very small dot, like the point of a pin.
fact: As an adjective, «pinpoint» means very exact, as in «pinpoint accuracy».
fact: Maps, science and detective stories use pinpoint: you pinpoint a town on a map, the cause of a problem, or a clue.
exercise: In «The cat turned its ear to pinpoint the squeak of a mouse», what does pinpoint mean? | To make a very small hole | To go to sleep | *To find the exact place of a sound | To jump very high
exercise: In «a pinpoint of light in the dark sky», what is a pinpoint? | A sharp pin used for maps | A large, bright lamp | *A very small dot of light | A loud noise
exercise: «The archer's pinpoint aim hit the centre every time.» What does pinpoint mean here? | *Very exact | Very slow | Very noisy | Very old
test: «The doctor will pinpoint the cause of the pain.» What does pinpoint mean? | *To find the exact cause | To shout the cause out loud | To paint the cause | To hide the cause
test: In «The coach praised her pinpoint pass», what does pinpoint mean? | *Very accurate | Very late | Very small | Very loud
exam: Jayden says pinpoint is always a verb. Is he right? | Yes, it is always a verb | Yes, but only when it is used on maps | No, it is always a noun | *No, it can be a verb, a noun or an adjective
